7.  NO WARRANTY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

7.1  EXCEPT FOR THE EXPRESS REPRESENTATION IN SECTION 3.4, THE MODEL AND CODE
     ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
     INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION ANY WARRANTY OF TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT,
     MERCHANTABILITY OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.

7.2  In particular, the Author makes no representation that:

     (a)  the Model is free of third-party claims arising from the provenance
          of its training data;

     (b)  the Model is accurate. Reported performance is 48% top-1 and 82%
          top-5 on 150 held-out clips across 50 classes, against 2% and 10%
          chance baselines. These are noisy point estimates: the standard error
          on the top-1 figure is roughly 4 points, and re-dealing the split
          moves it over a range of about 9 points. Read the headline as
          "roughly one in two", not as 0.480. Performance degrades on ensemble
          recordings, on fragments shorter than about 20 seconds, and on any
          raag outside the 50-class vocabulary — there is no "not a raag"
          output, so the Model will return a confident wrong answer rather than
          abstain;

     (c)  the tonic supplied to the Model is correct. The Model requires the
          tonic as an input and its output is only as good as that estimate; or

     (d)  the 50-class vocabulary is a representative or balanced sample of
          Hindustani raags. The training corpus is small and unevenly
          distributed across classes, and the Model's behaviour reflects that.

7.3  TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE AUTHOR SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR
     ANY CLAIM, DAMAGE OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT OR
     OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE MODEL, THE CODE, OR
     THEIR USE.


